# Direction

Base-direction provider for right-to-left locales. Roving navigation in every primitive reads it first, so mirrored arrows work with no `dir` attributes on the widgets themselves — including portaled content that escapes the DOM subtree. The provider still renders `dir` for native layout.

<div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border bg-card p-6 text-card-foreground">
	<Direction.Root direction="rtl">
		<Tabs.Root bind:value>
			<Tabs.List activation="automatic" class="flex gap-1 border-b">
				<Tabs.Trigger
					value="a"
					class="border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-1.5 text-sm data-[state=active]:border-primary"
				>
					Alpha
				</Tabs.Trigger>
				<Tabs.Trigger
					value="b"
					class="border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-1.5 text-sm data-[state=active]:border-primary"
				>
					Beta
				</Tabs.Trigger>
				<Tabs.Trigger
					value="c"
					class="border-b-2 border-transparent px-3 py-1.5 text-sm data-[state=active]:border-primary"
				>
					Gamma
				</Tabs.Trigger>
			</Tabs.List>
			<Tabs.Content value="a"><p>Panel A</p></Tabs.Content>
			<Tabs.Content value="b"><p>Panel B</p></Tabs.Content>
			<Tabs.Content value="c"><p>Panel C</p></Tabs.Content>
		</Tabs.Root>
	</Direction.Root>
	<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Selected: {value} (Tab in, then <code class="rounded-md border bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.8em]">←</code> moves forward here — mirrored)</p>
</div>

## Anatomy

<CodeBlock code={anatomy} filename="App.svelte" />

## API reference

### Direction.Root

<ApiTable props={rootProps} />

Without a provider, widgets fall back to the closest `dir` attribute, then `document.dir`. Physical floating placements do not auto-mirror; choose explicit placements per direction.

## Keyboard interactions

- None of its own — it mirrors every roving widget inside: <Kbd>←</Kbd><Kbd>→</Kbd> swap meaning under `rtl`.
